            <title>[LU-12840] sanity-pcc test_16: unmount failed on busy target</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12840</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for S Buisson &amp;lt;sbuisson@ddn.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/41385fdc-ea2e-11e9-a0ba-52540065bddc" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/41385fdc-ea2e-11e9-a0ba-52540065bddc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_16 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;test_16 returned 32
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test fails because at the end it fails to unmount the target which happens to be busy:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;CMD: trevis-56vm2 umount -d /mnt/pcc.d16.sanity-pcc
trevis-56vm2: umount: /mnt/pcc.d16.sanity-pcc: target is busy.
trevis-56vm2:         (In some cases useful info about processes that use
trevis-56vm2:          the device is found by lsof(8) or fuser(1))
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;p&gt;VVVVVVV DO NOT REMOVE LINES BELOW, Added by Maloo for auto-association VVVVVVV&lt;br/&gt;
sanity-pcc test_16 - test_16 returned 32&lt;/p&gt;</description>
